9	Enrolled agent information for
10	former IRS employees
11	
12	  More In Tax Pros                                                                        +
13	
14	
15	
16	Certain former IRS employees can become an enrolled agent without taking the Special
17	Enrollment Examination by virtue of past experience with the IRS.
18	
19	Circular 230 specifies that such applicants "must have been regularly engaged in applying
20	and interpreting the provisions of the Internal Revenue Code and the regulations relating to
21	income, estate, gift, employment, or excise taxes."
22	
23	In general, the experience must include at least five years in one of these taxpayer-facing
24	field positions: appeals oﬀicer, special agent, revenue oﬀicer, revenue agent, tax specialist,
25	tax law specialist, or settlement oﬀicer. Three of the five qualifying years must have
26	occurred within the last five years prior to separation from the IRS.
27	
28	These requirements are intended to ensure the applicant's IRS experience provides him/her
29	with the same overall background as a public sector candidate who passes all three parts of
30	the SEE. If the former employee's IRS experience does not provide the same overall
31	background, enrollment will be restricted to a specific area of representation.
32	
33	
34	To apply for enrollment based on former IRS experience,
35	you must:
36	   Submit an application for enrollment within three (3) years from the date of your
37	   separation with the IRS, using Form 23 PDF ;
38	   include information regarding education, training, licenses, and work experience; and
39	   pass a background check to ensure that you have not engaged in any conduct that
40	   would justify the suspension or disbarment of an attorney, CPA, or enrolled agent from
41	   practice before the IRS. This check will be conducted on your behalf upon submission of
42	   Form 23 PDF .
